{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0173EiYHBASK4EqUzd34HUCE","type":"tool_result","content":"import Mathlib\n\nopen Real Set Nat\n\nnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2016_b4_solution : ℕ → ℝ := (fun n : ℕ => (2 * n)! / (4 ^ n * (n)!))\n/--\nLet $A$ be a $2n \\times 2n$ matrix, with entries chosen independently at random. Every entry is chosen to be $0$ or $1$, each with probability $1/2$. Find the expected value of $\\det(A-A^t)$ (as a function of $n$), where $A^t$ is the transpose of $A$.\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2016_b4\n  (n : ℕ) (npos : n ≥ 1)\n  (mats01 : Set (Matrix (Fin (2 * n)) (Fin (2 * n)) ℝ))\n  (hmats01 : mats01 = {A | ∀ i j : Fin (2 * n), A i j = 0 ∨ A i j = 1}) :\n  (∑' A : mats01, (A.1 - (Matrix.transpose A)).det) / mats01.ncard = putnam_2016_b4_solution n :=\nsorry","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"809cfd7f-cb95-42dc-a49d-16dee6513042","uuid":"299310e7-c019-4fb8-b6e8-2807680be957","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:55:46.559Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"import Mathlib\n\nopen Real Set Nat\n\nnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2016_b4_solution : ℕ → ℝ := (fun n : ℕ => (2 * n)! / (4 ^ n * (n)!))\n/--\nLet $A$ be a $2n \\times 2n$ matrix, with entries chosen independently at random. Every entry is chosen to be $0$ or $1$, each with probability $1/2$. Find the expected value of $\\det(A-A^t)$ (as a function of $n$), where $A^t$ is the transpose of $A$.\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2016_b4\n  (n : ℕ) (npos : n ≥ 1)\n  (mats01 : Set (Matrix (Fin (2 * n)) (Fin (2 * n)) ℝ))\n  (hmats01 : mats01 = {A | ∀ i j : Fin (2 * n), A i j = 0 ∨ A i j = 1}) :\n  (∑' A : mats01, (A.1 - (Matrix.transpose A)).det) / mats01.ncard = putnam_2016_b4_solution n :=\nsorry","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0173EiYHBASK4EqUzd34HUCE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
